  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes (8 of 8).\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never freed its slot, so the queue stalled. A job that throws synchronously, or returns a plain value, also broke the queue. Every job's outcome now frees its slot, whether it resolves, rejects or throws.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving too early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits for `running` to reach 0.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `resume()` started a single job. The scheduler now loops to fill every free slot.\n\nI added six regression tests to `test/queue.test.js`:\n- Recovery after a rejected job and after a synchronous throw.\n- Plain-value jobs.\n- `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs, resolving immediately when idle, and resolving after failed jobs.\n- `resume()` reaching concurrency 4.\n- `pause()` letting running jobs finish while starting no new ones.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
